cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "splatmorph: seamlessly-looping 3D Gaussian morphs via one transport functional"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "J"
    given-names: "Ameer"
year: 2026
url: "https://github.com/AmeerJ97/splatmorph"
abstract: >
  Two images in, one seamlessly-looping 3D Gaussian morph out. A single
  optimal-transport functional decides set membership, morph ordering,
  splat correspondence, and per-splat trajectory; verification gates
  (loop exactness, endpoint purity, boundary quietness) are checked on
  every render. Built on Apple's SHARP monocular Gaussian model
  (research license) and 3D Gaussian Splatting.
